3. P0 — REPLACE BROWSER-ONLY WAV DOWNLOAD WITH REAL ANDROID SAVING

Existing defect

"src/App.tsx" currently exports using:

const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
const a = document.createElement('a');
a.href = url;
a.download = exportName;
a.click();
URL.revokeObjectURL(url);

This does not verify that Android wrote any file.

The app then reports export success based on Blob size.

Mandatory correction

Implement a platform-aware "ExportDestinationService".

Detect:

- Browser
- PWA
- Android Capacitor

Browser

Use a supported browser save strategy, retaining a fallback for browsers without File System Access APIs.

Clean up object URLs at an appropriate point after the download action rather than revoking synchronously.

Android

Use a correctly integrated native Android save workflow.

Recommended approach:

- Android Storage Access Framework
- "ACTION_CREATE_DOCUMENT"
- "ActivityResultLauncher"
- "ContentResolver.openOutputStream()" or supported seekable file descriptor
- Safe MIME type
- User-selected destination

For WAV:

"audio/wav"

Do not depend on direct filesystem paths inside restricted Android storage.

Do not require broad storage permissions when the system document picker is sufficient.

Save transaction

1. User selects WAV export.
2. Render job completes and validates the PCM/WAV data.
3. Show Android document destination picker.
4. User selects destination.
5. Write bytes.
6. Flush and close file descriptor.
7. Check for write failure.
8. Reopen/inspect saved document where permissions permit.
9. Verify file size and header.
10. Report final URI, size and status.

If the user cancels the picker, the result is "cancelled", not "success".

Critical data-integrity rule

Do not mark export complete just because "Blob" exists.

Mark export complete only after the save has succeeded.

For large WAV files, support bounded-memory output rather than unnecessarily materializing an enormous Blob.

Where WAV headers require final sizes, use a suitable seekable temporary file, finalization step or a supported streaming format.

Do not expose a partially written WAV as completed.

